INTERPRETATION:
  The selected first/last-five channels alone are insufficient, even
  when every label has cap at least three.  In the deep cap-at-least-three
  box, however, either auxiliary reservoir separately sufficed in every
  tested row: the truncated indexed-equal-pair reservoir had minimum 30,
  and the positive-cut reservoir had minimum 8.  The former failed only
  in the shallow (m,o,r)=(4,4,2) stratum at the level-four witness above;
  the latter had negative shallow minima in three residual strata.  The
  complete disjoint-reservoir target stayed positive with minimum 2.

  The all-cut deep ceiling stayed positive with minimum 10.  Retaining
  only local supply failed (minimum -15), retaining the equal-pair supply
  stayed positive (minimum 3), and retaining only positive-cut supply
  failed (minimum -11).  Setting equal-pair supply to zero gave minimum
  20, while the explicit low-output-band lower bound gave minimum 12.
  These additional ablations isolate the indexed equal-pair reservoir
  and the low-output band used by the proposed deep analytic argument.

  This exact replay motivates a deep/shallow reservoir split in the
  unbounded Presburger certificate.  It is bounded discovery evidence,
  not a proof beyond level 20.

